// The absence of a target language, for output that needs no backing code.
// `--lang none` emits no program: the html platform builds a static site with
// inline JS, and the interpreter runs tests without generating anything.
//
// It has a package for the same reason every other target does — so the answer
// to "what does this target accept" is a declaration rather than a silence — and
// the answer is nothing. There is no code generated for a language to configure.
// Nor is there Go behind it: it is a package in lib/, and the translator html
// is handed for it translates nothing.
